  "body": "We would like to give synapse support for multiple OIDC identity providers. As a first step:\r\n * [x] the user would be prompted to choose one from the `/_matrix/client/r0/login/sso/redirect` page\r\n   * [x] give synapse the concept of an \"identity provider\", and refactor existing CAS, SAML and OIDC impls to match it\r\n   * [x] redirect to an IdP picker when more than one IdP exists\r\n   * [x] serve an IdP picker based on a template\r\n   * [ ] support multiple OIDC providers, each as a separate IdP (#9110)\r\n   * [x] write some tests\r\n * [x] for UIA, the user would be taken to whichever OIDC provider they had registered with. (#9081)\r\n * ~~login fallback needs to support picking a provider too~~ actually, this is better done once synapse supports MSC2858; moved to #9013\r\n\r\n",
